Subject: [#94-10-90] Uploads...

In the discussion of uploads so far I haven't heard mention of the need to
record the brain's electrical state as well as it's structure. To use the
overworked brain-computer analogy we would need to save the contents of RAM
as well as the net list or wiring diagram.  

The connection weights alone may not do it as synapses will be firing away
and a simulation may have to be jump-started with billions of accurately
placed and timed impulses. Or does the brain have a "reboot" mechanism that
insures it continues to function after a glitch?  I'm imagining a
concussion, electrical shock or coma may trigger some such built in defense
mechanism built into the brain's structure.  Does anyone know?


