From: Chris Jaeb <cameron@netcom.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Oct 1994 19:22:37 -0700 (PDT)
Subject: [#94-10-91] Julian Jaynes

Deepak Chopra writes:

What is a thought?

It is an impulse of engery and information, like everything else
in Nature.

Being able to process the raw, chaotic vibrations of the "quantum
soup" and turn them into meaningful, orderly bits of relity opens
up enormous creative posisbilties. However, these possibilities
exist only when you are aware of them.

Thoughts come from nature. Your body/mind is a receiving
instrument that processes, at a subconsious level, a wide range
of external stimuli.  

Depending on what you are consciously giving priority to
at a specific place in time, you become aware of those 
thoughts. Meaning, constant "consciously" evolving, interrelated
shifts in awareness produce the verbalization of the energy/
information that is floating around in the environment.         

Chopra calls this floating "energy/information" the "vibrations
of the 'quantum soup'". Where the 'quantum soup' is the infinite
space from which all energy/thought is emitted. If you take any
object, from human bones to a rock, when you go beyond the
molecules, atoms, and electrons and get down to the quantum
level, there is certain intelligence that acts as the glue that
holds the atoms and molecules together and makes a human bone a
bone, and a rock a rock.

In other words, at a quantum level, we are all the same stuff, a
level of intelligence in the space time continuum that creates
unique objects and energy fields. So when you process a thought,
you are simply becoming aware of an impulse of energy in nature
and yourself. 

Real growth comes when you recognize the you do not live in this
world...this world lives in you! You begin seeing every thought
as a result of nature. And in a short time you develop more
control over your mind, become more intuned with nature, and can
more easily effect the natural evolution of mankind.

                                             cameron@netcom.com

